{"schemaVersion":1,"systemCode":"DIN:ara-Arab:Latn:31635-2011","dependencies":[],"metadata":{"authority_id":"din","id":"31635-2011","language":"iso-639-2:ara","source_script":"Arab","destination_script":"Latn","name":"DIN 31635:2011-07 Transliteration des arabischen Alphabets","url":"https://www.din.de","creation_date":"2011","confirmation_date":"2011-07","description":"DIN 31635:2011-07, section 6: transliteration of the Arabic alphabet, applicable\n    to classical and modern standard Arabic. Based on the 1935 recommendation of the\n    International Orientalists' Congress and nearly identical to ISO 233:1984, with\n    additional provisions in the notes for transliteration work. The norm's Persian,\n    Kurdish and Urdu sections are separate maps; its Ottoman-Turkish section gives\n    references only.","notes":["Vowel system (6.1.1): short vowels a, i, u; long vowels a-macron, i-macron, u-macron; diphthongs au, ai.","The Arabic article (6.1.2): the article forms are transliterated only with the short vowel a; the assimilation of the article consonant l to the sun letters is expressed (al-, ad-, an-, ar-, as-, at-, az- and the diacritic-modified ad-, adh-, at-, ath-, as-, ash-, az-); the article is always joined to the following word by a hyphen. This map renders the word-initial article with the hyphen and the sun-letter assimilation; the elision of the article's a after a vowel-final preceding word (rule d) and the loss of length in a preceding long vowel (rule e) require the vocalization of the preceding word and are not implemented; the exception of the word Allah is lexical and not implemented.","Individual remarks (6.1.3): (a) sukun is never transliterated; (b) tashdid is expressed by doubling the consonant under the shadda, this map implements the doubled renderings for every consonant letter, while the shadda combinations with waw (-uw, -auw-) and ya (-iy, -aiy-, word-finally -i after i) are vocalization-dependent and not implemented; (c) the rendering of alif is omitted word-initially; (d) the rendering of hamza is omitted word-initially; (e) the hamza carriers alif, waw and ya are not transliterated as such - the hamza renders as the right half-ring and the carrier letter contributes nothing, so hamza-plus-short-vowel-mark renders the mark's vowel; (f) alif with madda renders as a-macron, word-internally as right-half-ring plus a-macron; (g) alif maqsura renders as a-macron; (h) hamzat al-wasl elision behavior requires the preceding context's vocalization and is not implemented; (i) the pausal form is transliterated: nunation and short final vowels fall, with the exception of the accusative ending -an of indeterminate nouns and adjectives - this map renders fathatan as an and the other tanwin forms as empty, per the remark's default; (j) the completion of case endings of verbs, pronouns, suffixes and prepositions is grammatical and not implemented; (k) the hyphenation rules for particles are syntactic and not implemented; (l) ta marbuta after the long vowel a-macron renders h, otherwise it is not expressed (the construct-state -t is morphological and not implemented).","Waw and ya (rows 27 and 28) render as consonant w / y by default; over vocalized input the long-vowel renderings u-macron / i-macron apply via the vowel-mark combinations. Unvocalized text is an underspecified skeleton: the waw/ya long-vowel readings, the article elision and the pausal forms are resolved by a vocalization model, after which this map applies (composition, not duplication).","Transliteration is not aimed at being reversible (section 4); for alphabetical ordering the diacritics and apostrophes are not considered (section 5)."]},"stages":[{"kind":"stage","name":"main","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ْ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":""}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"َّ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"َّ"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ِّ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"ِّ"}}